WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.869
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.403
We hope you're doing well.
And now, if you don't mind,

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:06.739
we're going to get to the news.
President Biden visited

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:10.442
an Amtrak maintenance facility
today in Delaware.

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:12.779
So we got an extra hour
of sleep this weekend,

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.782
but he sure didn't.
"I'm too excited."

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:21.153
Former President Trump
took the witness stand today

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:23.890
in his civil fraud trial.
He swore to tell the truth,

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.792
the whole truth and nothing
but the truth,

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:28.495
and then everyone
just laughed and laughed.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.999
While testifying during his
civil fraud trial today,

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.266
former President Trump said

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:35.935
that he believes
his Mar a Lago resort

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.305
is worth between
$1 billion and $1.5 billion.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.640
Oh. Very smart.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.543
The insanity defense.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:47.980
Dude, you bought it
for $10,000,000 in 1985,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.884
and now it's worth 1.5 billion?

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:55.488
The only way I would believe
that is if it was in Brooklyn.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:59.025
Then that's about right.
Maybe a little low.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.259
While testifying today,

00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.094
former President Trump
also appeared to forget

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.430
that he wasn't president
in 2021.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.802
Well, so did half the country.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.037
After FBI agents raided the home

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.972
of his chief fundraiser
last week,

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.808
New York Mayor Eric Adams said,
quote,

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.277
"Where there's smoke,
there's not always fire."

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:23.282
Ah, yes,
that famous expression.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.250
Okay, so we found out
he's shady.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.855
But you know what they say --
late is worse than never.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.895
The third Republican
presidential primary debate

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.497
will be held Wednesday in Miami
or, as it's now dubbed,

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:42.601
"Who Wants to Be
a Vice President?"

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.337
Pennsylvania Senator
John Fetterman

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.873
criticized California Governor
Gavin Newsom over the weekend

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.808
and said he was secretly
running for president,

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.176
as opposed to Fetterman,

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.377
who looks like
he's running for

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:54.380
guy who doesn't wipe down
the equipment at the gym.

00:01:57.416 --> 00:02:00.686
Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg
revealed on Friday

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.622
that he tore his ACL
while training

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.490
for a competitive MMA fight.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.359
Apparently,
what happened was

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.995
there was a coffee table
in the way.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.070
The fastest runner in
the New York City Marathon

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.371
yesterday
finished the course

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.239
in just under two hours
and five minutes,

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:26.145
a full ten minutes faster
than if he had taken the bus.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:30.749
Better luck next year, the bus.

00:02:30.749 --> 00:02:33.119
Archeologists in Germany believe
they've discovered

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.754
the ancient remains
of a husband and wife

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:37.757
buried in the same casket.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.192
Her idea.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.463
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.266
Baz!

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.671
We're going to win them back
with this one.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.907
And finally, the American
Ornithological -- Ornith--

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.709
Oh, Jesus.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.477
I said this word wrong
last week,

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:01.581
and I got a lot of angry notes
from ornithologists.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:05.418
And now I'm in my head about it.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.887
And finally, the American
Bird People Society

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.588
announced --
It's fine.

00:03:09.588 --> 00:03:15.428
It's an either/or.
It's famously an either/or.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:18.164
Announced last week that it
is renaming birds

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.733
that are currently named
after problematic people,

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.835
though in retrospect,
it was never really fair

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.836
to name that one

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.137
Jared from Subway.

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:28.907
And... that was a monologue,
everybody.

00:03:28.907 --> 00:03:29.943
We're up and running.

